Went back to The Crocodile on Saturday night for Day 2 of Go! Machine. This time equipped with a Minolta Hi-Matic AF2 I chanced upon earlier in the day at Value Village for $2.99. Didn&#8217;t have time to cop some film, so I dug around the crib and found an old roll of Kodak Max [...]]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-968" title="63220023 (1)" src="http://bluescholars.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/63220023-1.jpg" alt="63220023 (1)" width="500" height="331" /></p>
<p>Went back to The Crocodile on Saturday night for Day 2 of <strong>Go! Machine</strong>. This time equipped with a <strong>Minolta Hi-Matic AF2</strong> I chanced upon earlier in the day at Value Village for $2.99. Didn&#8217;t have time to cop some film, so I dug around the crib and found an old roll of Kodak Max 800 (@ 400 ISO) that expired in 2006. One annoying little quirk about this camera: the flash (which is a mighty one) takes about 10-15 seconds to charge up. And it gives an annoying continuous beep if you&#8217;re too far away from a subject. So every shot was up close. Some too close&#8211;the flash turning some of yall into pasty ghosts. Many were pasty ghosts to begin with. I drank significantly less than the night before and the camera was too big to fit in the pocket and occasionally forget about. So I got trigger happy and ran out of film before <strong>Mad Rad</strong> hit the stage. All good, though. That&#8217;s something you have to see for yourself anyway. Go forth and see more photos after the jump:</p>
